    "final_answer": "# Latest iPad Model Specifications\n\nBased on my navigation through apple.com, the **latest iPad model** released by Apple is the **iPad Pro (M5)**, available in two sizes. Here are its detailed specifications:\n\n## Models\n- **iPad Pro 11-inch (M5)**\n- **iPad Pro 13-inch (M5)**\n\n## Storage Options (Capacity)\nBoth the 11-inch and 13-inch models are available in:\n- **256GB**\n- **512GB**\n- **1TB**\n- **2TB**\n\n## Processor Type\n- **Apple M5 chip**\n  - 9-core CPU with 3 super cores and 6 efficiency cores (on 256GB / 512GB models)\n  - 10-core GPU with Neural Accelerators\n  - Hardware-accelerated ray tracing\n  - 16-core Neural Engine\n\n## Display Features\n**11-inch model:**\n- Ultra Retina XDR display\n- Tandem OLED\n- 2420-by-1668-pixel resolution at 264 ppi\n- ProMotion technology with adaptive refresh rates from 10Hz to 120Hz\n- Wide color (P3)\n- True Tone\n- Fingerprint-resistant oleophobic coating\n- Fully laminated\n- Antireflective coating\n- Nano-texture display glass option on 1TB and 2TB models\n- SDR brightness: 1000 nits max\n- XDR brightness: 1000 nits max full screen, 1600 nits peak (HDR content only)\n- 1 nit minimum brightness\n- 2,000,000:1 contrast ratio\n- Supports Apple Pencil Pro, Apple Pencil (USB-C), and Apple Pencil hover\n\n**13-inch model:**\n- Ultra Retina XDR display\n- Tandem OLED\n- 2752-by-2064-pixel resolution at 264 ppi\n- ProMotion technology with adaptive refresh rates from 10Hz to 120Hz\n- Wide color (P3)\n- True Tone\n- Fingerprint-resistant oleophobic coating\n- Fully laminated\n- Antireflective coating\n- Same brightness/contrast specs as the 11-inch model\n- Supports Apple Pencil Pro, Apple Pencil (USB-C), and Apple Pencil hover\n\n## Source\nInformation retrieved from: **https://www.apple.com/ipad-pro/specs/**",
